{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"foldable-gaseous-owl","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nDiscovered while triaging breezy-hogged-mastiff, which owns `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/unclassified.args`. These 41 entries move to `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/path-separators.args`, which this bug owns.\n\nSome cases are product output that should be POSIX-form: the agent `search_files` tool prints `pkg\\alpha.py:2:` (`test_pai_tools_search_files_bf31.py`, `test_pydantic_ai_runner.py`), the compaction intent journal records `<tid>\\x-SNAPSHOT.json` (`test_compact_crash_atomicity.py`), and the code-review prompt error names `.rebar\\prompts\\...` (`test_code_review_project_criteria.py`). Others are test fakes or expectations: the replacement-walker fake reducer splits paths on `/` while the product joins with `os.path.join` (`tests/unit/commands/test_replacement_walker.py:33`), the AST-guard tests compare `relative_to` output with `jira_family/` (`test_jira_family_boundary.py`, `test_rich_text_seam.py`), and POSIX container paths pass through `Path` (`test_gate_scratch_volume_aa40.py::test_autodeploy_mcp_run_new_routes_gate_scratch_to_the_parent_bind`).\n\nEvidence: Windows runs on throwaway branch `tmp/w05-remeasure` with origin/main `717c50f8b33` code plus a selection-only workflow change: run 44665461131 (the 242 `unclassified.args` entries; 48 passed, 194 failed or errored) and run 44681457334 (the 194, xdist, JUnit XML with full tracebacks). Both 2026-11-19 PST.\n\nModules:\n- `tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py` (1)\n- `tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py` (2)\n- `tests/unit/commands/test_replacement_walker.py` (5)\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/mutate/test_inbound_status_cascade.py` (2)\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/orchestrate/test_reconcile_once.py` (1)\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/test_jira_family_boundary.py` (3)\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/test_rich_text_seam.py` (2)\n- `tests/unit/test_check_templatefile_escapes.py` (2)\n- `tests/unit/test_code_review_project_criteria.py` (2)\n- `tests/unit/test_compact_crash_atomicity.py` (2)\n- `tests/unit/test_criteria_snapshot.py` (1)\n- `tests/unit/test_gate_scratch_volume_aa40.py` (1)\n- `tests/unit/test_pai_tools_search_files_bf31.py` (5)\n- `tests/unit/test_project_review_phase_boundaries.py` (1)\n- `tests/unit/test_prompt_repo_root_seam.py` (4)\n- `tests/unit/test_pydantic_ai_runner.py` (1)\n- `tests/unit/test_relocated_store_repo_root.py` (1)\n- `tests/unit/test_user_data_size_a68c.py` (4)\n- `tests/unit/test_worktree_config_root.py` (1)\n\n## Approach\nEmit repo-relative paths with `as_posix()` at the product boundaries named above (the same rule as commit `f163c9c987f`), and fix the test-side comparisons. Remove each line from `path-separators.args` as it passes.\n\n## Scope\nTest or product code for the listed modules, plus `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/path-separators.args` (remove each fixed line; delete the file and its `@` reference in `.github/workflows/test.yml` once empty).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every line removed from `path-separators.args` names a test that passed in a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the fix (run id recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] `path-separators.args` is empty and deleted with its reference in `.github/workflows/test.yml`, or each remaining line names a test recorded on this ticket as intentionally unsupported on Windows with the reason.\n","id":"7a2d-9166-ce30-4c1d","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":["windows","portability"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows sweep: 41 tests still compare backslash paths with forward-slash expectations"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1795154021446724001,"uuid":"b558d30f-ff26-4b40-955f-c89228266dee"}